== a plain function reply keeps its text:
probe_dir
probe_file
== -o filenames marks the directory reply:
probe_dir/
probe_file
== compopt +o filenames turns the mark off:
probe_dir
== compopt +o filenames turns the -d mark off:
probe_dir
== compopt +o filenames turns the -f mark off:
probe_dir
probe_file
== compopt +o filenames turns the -G mark off:
probe_dir
probe_file
== -o dirnames marks the directories it adds after the function:
probe_dir/
== -o plusdirs marks the directories it adds after the function:
probe_dir/
== -o filenames marks a word list directory:
probe_dir/
probe_file
== complete -p prints the option:
complete -o filenames -W 'probe_dir' cp
